      "title": "Risk Data Accuracy, Integrity and Reconciliation",
      "statement": "The bank shall aggregate risk data in a way that is accurate and reliable, applying controls to risk data that are at least as robust as those applied to accounting data. The bank shall strive to maintain a single authoritative source for each type of risk data. The bank shall reconcile risk data to its source systems and, where appropriate, to accounting data, and shall record the reference and result of each reconciliation. Where manual processes or desktop applications are used in risk data aggregation, the bank shall document those processes, maintain end-user computing controls consistently across all such processes, and record the rationale and criticality of any manual workaround. The bank shall measure and monitor data accuracy and shall maintain escalation channels and remediation plans to address poor data quality.",
